{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"What moved. Every other tool here quotes today's price; this one says whether it has just changed, from the price archive optimtoken.optimnow.io keeps (its first day is `provenance.trackingStart`). Without `models` it returns the moves of the last 7 days across the catalogue: each model whose quoted price moved by 1% or more, with the price before and after and what the move does to a workload's monthly bill. With `models` (1-4 names) it returns each model's quoted price since tracking began, change by change. Use it for 'did any LLM price change this week', 'which models got cheaper', 'has the price of X moved since the summer', 'is this price stable enough to budget on'. Read the flags: most models are sold by several hosts and one of them is quoted, so a move flagged `hostSwitch` is a change of the host quoted, not a repricing, and `outlierHost` is an outlier listing. The moves with no flag are returned apart, as `priceChanges`; no flag means none was established, which is not proof that the model maker repriced. There is no fallback for this data: when the archive cannot be read the tool returns an error, never an empty list that would read as 'nothing moved'.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"direction":{"description":"Week's moves only: keep the rises (up) or the falls (down). Not accepted with `models`.","enum":["up","down"],"type":"string"},"includeFlagged":{"description":"Week's moves only: false leaves out the moves flagged as a change of quoted host or an outlier listing. Default: true, returned apart in `flaggedMoves`. Not accepted with `models`.","type":"boolean"},"limit":{"description":"Week's moves: max moves returned in each of the two groups, largest first. History: max changes printed per model, the most recent (structuredContent carries all). Default: 15","maximum"